      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Adverb"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "An adverb modifies or qualifies a verb, an adjective, or another adverb, specifying details like manner, place, time, frequency, or degree.",
        "Adverbs of Manner describe how an action occurs (e.g., carefully, swiftly).",
        "Adverbs of Frequency indicate how often an action happens (e.g., always, seldom, usually).",
        "Adverbs of Degree express the intensity or extent of a quality or action (e.g., very, completely, extremely).",
        "Comparison of adverbs follows three degrees: Positive, Comparative, and Superlative (e.g., fast, faster, fastest)."
      ],
      "id": "rxgvjj0"
    },
