    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Avoid using double negatives with negative adverbs such as 'hardly', 'scarcely', 'barely', and 'rarely'.",
        "Apply the Rule of Inversion: When a sentence starts with a negative adverb, place the auxiliary verb before the subject (e.g., 'Seldom have I seen such dedication').",
        "Position the adverb 'only' directly before the specific word or phrase it is intended to modify to avoid ambiguity."
      ],
      "id": "kc5xayz"
